    {
      "@type": "ScholarlyArticle",
      "@id": "https://yassiralkarawi.github.io/research/cybersecure-entangled-qnn-ris-qkd.html#article",
      "headline": "Cybersecure Synchronisation of Entangled Quantum Neural Networks With Reconfigurable Intelligent Surface and Quantum Key Distribution for 6G Holographic Communications",
      "name": "Cybersecure Synchronisation of Entangled Quantum Neural Networks With Reconfigurable Intelligent Surface and Quantum Key Distribution for 6G Holographic Communications",
      "description": "A secure synchronisation framework combining entangled quantum neural networks, reconfigurable intelligent surfaces, and quantum key distribution for 6G holographic communications. The proposed hybrid quantum–classical framework coordinates distributed quantum neural networks for 6G holographic communications. It combines entanglement-assisted synchronisation, reconfigurable intelligent surfaces and quantum key distribution within a single communication and learning model. GHZ-state gradient consensus and entropy- and trace-distance regularisation support synchronisation. QNN parameters and RIS phases are jointly adjusted to preserve fidelity under noise, with QKD protecting the modelled midhaul. Qiskit simulations compare the full framework with reduced versions that omit GHZ synchronisation or RIS assistance. Across 100 simulation trials, the abstract reports mean fidelity of 0.961 and latency of 22.5 ms. Fidelity improvements of 20–28% are reported relative to the reduced baselines. The reported evidence is simulation-based; these figures do not establish an operational 6G holographic network or experimentally demonstrated security.",
      "datePublished": "2026-01",
      "dateModified": "2026-09-07",
      "inLanguage": "en",
      "creativeWorkStatus": "Published",
      "author": [
