    {
      "@type": "ScholarlyArticle",
      "@id": "https://yassiralkarawi.github.io/research/off-grid-oran-ris-edge-energy.html#article",
      "headline": "Energy-Aware Optimisation for Off-Grid ORAN With RIS and Edge Computing",
      "name": "Energy-Aware Optimisation for Off-Grid ORAN With RIS and Edge Computing",
      "description": "An energy-aware optimisation framework for off-grid Open RAN that integrates reconfigurable intelligent surfaces and edge computing. The paper studies solar-powered Open RAN in isolated environments, combining reconfigurable intelligent surfaces and mobile edge computing. The resource-management problem must accommodate changing harvested energy and traffic while respecting delay, power and temperature limits. A primal–dual controller updates transmit power, CPU speed and RIS phases from queue and energy conditions. The objective balances energy use, delay, SINR-related reliability and fairness. MATLAB simulations, sensitivity analysis and ablation tests examine the individual design choices. The abstract reports 25% lower energy consumption and 18% lower average delay than the baseline under the simulated solar and traffic conditions. The source identifies the evidence as MATLAB simulation, not field measurements from an off-grid network. Reported gains apply to the evaluated baseline and constraints.",
      "datePublished": "2025-01",
      "dateModified": "2026-09-07",
      "inLanguage": "en",
      "creativeWorkStatus": "Published",
      "author": [
