    {
      "@type": "ScholarlyArticle",
      "@id": "https://yassiralkarawi.github.io/research/trade-offs-5g-networks-beyond.html#article",
      "headline": "On the Trade-offs of 5G Networks and Beyond",
      "name": "On the Trade-offs of 5G Networks and Beyond",
      "description": "An examination of engineering trade-offs that shape fifth-generation mobile networks and their evolution beyond 5G. The paper examines green mobile-network design as a set of competing engineering and economic objectives. Energy efficiency is considered alongside deployment cost and service performance, rather than as an isolated target. Numerical analysis examines relationships involving power, bandwidth, spectral efficiency, delay, carbon emissions, deployment cost and revenue. The scope connects technical network choices with the cost considerations faced by operators and investors. The work highlights trade-offs between greener operation and cost efficiency. Its abstract does not establish a single configuration that is optimal for every network, or give a universal percentage improvement.",
      "datePublished": "2021-03-16",
      "dateModified": "2026-09-07",
      "inLanguage": "en",
      "creativeWorkStatus": "Published",
      "author": [
        {
